  "cap": "Im} H_t$ and the colour $\\arg H_t$ (bar); $H_t$ is drawn on 5 surfaces, one for each of the sheets $k=-2,\\dots,2$ of $F$. Each deformed logarithm runs along $(z^{u}e^{2\\pi iku}-1)/u+u$, $u=1-t$, where $k$ is its branch number on that surface. Shown at $t=1.00$, where $H_t=f_{2}\\circ G_t$ deforms $f_{2}$ ($t=0$) into $F(z)=\\sin\\left(\\log z\\right)$ ($t=1$); it is the homotopy $H_t=f_{2}\\circ G_t$, $0\\le t\\le 1$, where $G_t$ is the homotopy $G_t(z)=(z^{1-t}-1)/(1-t)+1-t$ for $0\\le t<1$, $G_1(z)=\\log z$ (on every sheet). Here $F=f_{2}\\circ f_{1}$ with $f_{1}(z)=\\log z$ and $f_{2}(w)=\\sin w$. On its natural domain $D=\\{z : \\arg z\\neq 180^\\circ\\}$, $F$ is analytic; this is guaranteed by the chain."
 },
